      "message": "During PD Policies testing, I\u0027ve noticed the firmware_PDResetHard test was failing, even with stock firmware. After debugging, it turned out there is an issue with sync between pd_task and pd_interrupt_handler_task. After receiving a hard reset command, pd_interrupt_handler_task calls pd_execute_hard_reset, which changes task_state and last_state, but due to the sleep in nx20p348x_vbus_source_enable the function is not executed completely, then pd_task is resumed with no notification that pd_execute_hard_reset is being executed.\nI\u0027ve checked how it is solved on master - the bug has just been fixed with these two commits CL:1389992 CL:2284504\n\n",
